omponents is a bare list), no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were taken from architecture context (KServe → RHOAI Serving, Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard).\n- **Priority inversion risk (informational):** HLR-4 is labeled P2 yet the strategy itself states HLR-1 (P0) cannot ship before the schema is settled — the schema epic is promoted to P0 via priority inheritance. The HLR-4 label understates its blocking nature.\n- **Scope trap (informational):** HLR-2's \"not lost on component restart\" implies transient local buffering of undelivered events inside KServe. Long-term storage and retention are explicitly out of scope (customer-provided); the epic must treat buffering as delivery reliability only, not a storage subsystem.\n- **Docs epic ownership unspecified:** The strategy names no documentation owner. RHOAI Serving is assigned as the feature owner; a human should confirm whether a dedicated documentation team takes this epic.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- KServe and Dashboard are canonical components in `.context/rhai-components.txt` and both have architecture context files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`, `dashboard.md`) — no onboarding chain required; both are Konflux-onboarded per architecture context, so no konflux-onboarding epic or \"build pipeline green\" AC (Rule 25) is generated.\n- The docs epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component. Documentation has no architecture context file, but it is a docs work-product epic (`implementation_type: docs-authoring`), not a code component — the new-component onboarding rule does not apply.\n\n## Investigation Epics\n\nNone. The strategy explicitly states open questions are none, and the audit sink interface is identified as the standard cluster logging forwarder. No conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or unknowns that would change which epics exist. The buffering mechanism for at-least-once delivery and the enable/disable propagation mechanism are implementation details (acceptance criteria on E002/E003), not genuine unknowns.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. No external dependency with uncertain timing: the audit sink is the in-cluster standard logging forwarder, and no upstream contributions are required.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input\n\nNo Staff Engineer Input section is present in the strategy; decomposition follows the strategy body.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25166,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b0a662afd2f09df","agent_id":"a0954d66229d27e1c","session_id":"2216ab2c-51dc-48a5-83cb-2b16959bc098","uuid":"ad1492c8-a621-4679-8140-c80088de4777","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:58:25.251Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
