{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9928b087-4641-41fa-bffe-b72b2e6ce1da","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb2c9c310dcbaa41","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9010-vtcsvjs2/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9010-E001.md","content":"# Define and publish the common inference audit event schema\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic defines and publishes the common audit event schema for inference traffic on RHOAI. The schema is the platform-level contract that inference audit events must conform to and that future components (pipelines, workbenches) will adopt in later strategies so their events remain compatible. It is a design-and-publication deliverable, not a code change in the serving path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define a structured audit event schema capturing, per inference request: caller identity, model and version, timestamp, and response status.\n- Explicitly exclude request/response payloads from the schema (audit events carry metadata only).\n- Ensure the schema is expressible through the standard cluster logging forwarder, which is the cluster audit sink.\n- Publish the schema in a location and form that downstream components and future strategies can consume and extend.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The schema defines fields for caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status, and mandates that no payload content is carried in audit events.\n- The schema is validated against the delivery path of the standard cluster logging forwarder (events structured per the schema can be forwarded to the cluster audit sink).\n- The schema is published and referenced such that a future component (e.g., pipelines, workbenches) could emit compatible events without further negotiation of the format.\n- The strategy's requirement that inference audit events cannot ship before the schema is settled is satisfied: the schema is settled and available before emission work completes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2, promoted to P0 via priority inheritance)** — a common audit event schema is defined and published so future components emit compatible events. This epic is the complete delivery of HLR-4 and is the prerequisite for the P0 inference audit emission requirement (HLR-1).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27849,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b0a662afd2f09df","agent_id":"a0954d66229d27e1c","session_id":"2216ab2c-51dc-48a5-83cb-2b16959bc098","uuid":"3595d837-507b-4b87-b4af-55b7274b2805","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:58:40.392Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
