{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bc1cff9c-a5aa-443d-b638-849992e99ee4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f59a151b1ddfd7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9010-vtcsvjs2/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9010-E003.md","content":"# Per-project inference auditing toggle in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic adds administrator-facing controls in the RHOAI Dashboard to enable and disable inference auditing per project. It gives administrators the self-service switch required for compliance-scoped deployments, building on the per-project audit enablement configuration that the serving-side inference auditing capability reads.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a per-project control in the Dashboard that administrators use to enable or disable inference auditing for that project.\n- Wire the control to the serving-side audit enablement configuration so the toggle takes effect on the inference path.\n- Restrict the control to project administrators (consistent with the Dashboard's OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a user with project administrator permissions, when they open the inference auditing settings for a project, then they can enable and disable inference auditing for that project.\n- Given auditing is enabled for a project via the Dashboard, when inference requests are served in that project, then audit events are emitted; given it is disabled, then no events are emitted for that project.\n- Given a user without administrator permissions on a project, when they view the project in the Dashboard, then the inference auditing toggle is not available to them.\n- The toggle's state reflects the actual serving-side audit enablement configuration for the project.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard.\n"}}],"m