ormance, at-least-once delivery with restart survival, and enable/disable behavior — each traceable to an HLR. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID; cross-epic references use descriptive phrases (\"the Dashboard work\", \"the serving-side audit enablement configuration\").\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe combined epic set covers the full strategy scope: event emission with the four required fields and payload exclusion (E002), at-least-once delivery and restart survival (E002), per-project admin toggle (E003), published common schema for future components (E001), and enablement/interpretation documentation (E004). Strategy-level context is carried forward rather than dropped: the out-of-scope boundaries (non-inference traffic, customer-provided retention) appear in E002's scope and E004's scope; the future-strategy adoption of the schema appears in E001's description; the tamper-evident/structured requirement appears in E002's description. No conditional branches are used and none are needed (no bounded unknowns). The docs-authoring requirement (HLR-5) has a corresponding docs epic, satisfying Rule 11.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24331,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94597b3738fec048","agent_id":"a5076f2e00e677d4c","session_id":"2216ab2c-51dc-48a5-83cb-2b16959bc098","uuid":"51bfc899-129a-4060-ba27-78d51b911281","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:04:08.489Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
