{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ac694f6ce9be1a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E003\n3\ttitle: Per-project inference auditing toggle in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Per-project inference auditing toggle in the Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic adds administrator-facing controls in the RHOAI Dashboard to enable and disable inference auditing per project. It gives administrators the self-service switch required for compliance-scoped deployments, building on the per-project audit enablement configuration that the serving-side inference auditing capability reads.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Add a per-project control in the Dashboard that administrators use to enable or disable inference auditing for that project.\n39\t- Wire the control to the serving-side audit enablement configuration so the toggle takes effect on the inference path.\n40\t- Restrict the control to project administrators (consistent with the Dashboard's OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC).\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a user with project administrator permissions, when they open the inference auditing settings for a project, then they can enable and disable inference auditing for that project.\n45\t- Given auditing is enabled for a project via the Dashboard, when inference requests are served in that project, then audit events are emitted; given it is disabled, then no events are emitted for that project.\n46\t- Given a user without administrator permissions on a project, when they view the project in the Dashboard, then the inference auditing toggle is not available to them.\n47\t- The toggle's state reflects the actual serving-side audit enablement configuration for the project.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f4a43dc8f927cb3","agent_id":"a9794b1ea2b097c41","session_id":"2216ab2c-51dc-48a5-83cb-2b16959bc098","uuid":"654d2585-43e5-4218-a090-870828ab6ee1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:06:09.295Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ac694f6ce9be1a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
