 the documentation can enable inference auditing for a project and verify that events arrive at the cluster audit sink.\n47\t- A reader can interpret an audit event's fields against the published common inference audit event schema without additional support.\n48\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented inference auditing capability (emission, delivery semantics, and the Dashboard toggle) before publication.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-5 (P2)** — documentation covers enabling auditing and interpreting events.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f4a43dc8f927cb3","agent_id":"a9794b1ea2b097c41","session_id":"2216ab2c-51dc-48a5-83cb-2b16959bc098","uuid":"e39ba0f9-61aa-4e2f-ab2a-61244f6f034c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:06:10.035Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc3f1ec69abcd590","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
